 1. Exporting/releasing code
    ------------------------

Most important rule: treat unpublished code of others with respect = 
meaning do not release code of others without asking.

For CMake builds:
   $ ./pamadm --release [perhaps other flags]
   $ mkdir build
   $ cd build
   $ cmake ..
   $ make release

For configure builds:
   $ ./pamadm --release [perhaps other flags]
   $ ./configure
   $ make cbuild/Makefile.dep
   $ mkdir build
   $ cd build
   $ cmake ..
   $ make release


 2. What do I need to do to add/remove source files?
    ------------------------------------------------

New files are automatically added by pamadm which generates cmake/Sources.list


 3. How do I set compiler flags?
    ----------------------------

Compiler flags are set in cmake/Compilers.cmake. These flags control
compilation in release mode (with optimization; FLAGS_RELEASE; default in
./setup) or debug mode (without optimization; FLAGS_DEBUG; default when calling
cmake directly).


 4. Creating DEB, RPM, and other packages
    -------------------------------------

Configure and build the source, then:
   $ cpack -G DEB
or
   $ cpack -G RPM
Always use the help that is available:
   $ cpack --help
